.TITLE "rm"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Removes files or directories. it permanently deletes __filesystem objects__ and must be used with caution as there is no built-in undo for this operation.

.DIV "TLDR"
**rm file.txt**
Deletes a specific file from the system.
> __file.txt__ the file to remove

**rm -r directory/**
Deletes a directory and all of its contents recursively.
> __-r__ recursive flag | __directory/__ the target folder

**rm -f file.txt**
Forces the removal of a file without prompting for confirmation, even if it is write-protected.
> __-f__ force flag

**rm -v file.txt**
Displays the name of each file as it is being deleted.
> __-v__ verbose flag

**rm -i file.txt**
Prompts for confirmation before each file is deleted.
> __-i__ interactive flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Deleting files with __rm__ bypasses the macOS **Trash**. For critical system cleanup, combine __-r__ and __-f__ with extreme care to avoid accidental deletion of important data.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:cp** **mac:mv**

